    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="24.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 24.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="24.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="326" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.12-2"/> hit man þonne befo, ⁊ he þyllice<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.13"/> gewitnesse næbbe, ne beo þær nan team, ac agyfe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.14"/> man þa<hi rend="italic">m<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.15"/></hi> agenfrigan his agen ⁊ þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> æftergild<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.16"/>, ⁊ þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wite þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> þe hit áge.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="24.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="326" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gyf hit mon ðonne gefó, ⁊ he ðyllice gewitnysse næbbe, ne beo ðær nan team, ac gyfe man ðam agenfrigean his agen ⁊ þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> æft<hi rend="italic">er</hi>gyld, ⁊ þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wite ðam ðe hit áge.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="24.1" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="326" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gif hit man þonne befo, ⁊ he þillice gewittnysse nabbe, ne beo þar nan team, ac agife man þæt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.2"/> ágenfrigean his ægen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.1"/> ⁊ þæt æftergyld, ⁊ þa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.1"/> wite þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> þe hit age.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="24.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="327" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si tunc super eum intercietur, et tale testimonium non habeat, non liceat ei aduocare, sed reddat repetenti captale<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.11"/> suum et secundam solutionem, et forisfacturam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.12"/> cui pertinebit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="24.1" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="327" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si non tot nec tales testes habuerit, et aliquid tale in manu uel potestate eius inuentum fuerit, et ipse warantem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.11-2"/> uoluerit uocare, non<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.12-3"/> ei ualeat neque<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.13-2"/> liceat, sed reddatur calumnianti quod suum est — aut ualens — et insuper iterum tantum ualens, et forisfacturam qui eam iuste<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.14-2"/> habere debet.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="24.1" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="327" ed="#liebermann"/>Quodsi apud illum deprehensum fuerit, et huiusmodi testimonium non habuit, nulla sit aduocacio tutacionis, sed deprehensori suum reddat et prosolutam, et forisfacturam illi qui possidet.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="24.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="186" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ gyf hit mon ðonne gefó<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#IICn_24-1.robnote.fn.5"/> ⁊ he ðyllice gewitnysse næbbe, ne beo ðær nan team, ac gyfe man ðam agenfrigean his agen ⁊ þæt æftergyld ⁊ þæt wite ðam ðe hit áge.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="266" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gyf hit man þonne befo, and he þyllice gewitnesse næbbe, ne beo þær nan team, ac agyfe man þam agenfrigan his agen and þæt æftergild, and þæt wite þam þe hit age.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="327" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wenn es nachher im Anefang eingeklagt wird, und er [der verklagte Besitzer] solche Zeugenschaft nicht hat, so sei da kein Gewährzug [ihm erlaubt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_24-1.lnote.de.1"/>], sondern er gebe dem Eigenthümer dessen Eigen zurück sammt nochmaliger Werthzahlung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_24-1.lnote.de.2"/>, und das Strafgeld dem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_24-1.lnote.de.3"/>, der es [das Recht auf das vom Verklagten Verwirkte] besitzt.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if it is then attached, and he [the accused possessor] does not have such witness, let there be no vouching to warranty [allowed him], but let him give back to the owner his property together with a second payment of its value, and the fine to the one who owns it [the right to what the accused has forfeited].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="187" ed="#robertson"/>If, however, any property is attached, and he [who is in possession of it] has no such witnesses, no vouching to warranty shall be allowed, but the property shall be given up to its rightful owner and also the supplementary payment<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_24-1.robnote.n.1"/>, and the fine to the party who is entitled thereto.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="465" ed="#whitelock"/>And if it is then attached, and he has not such witness, there is to be no vouching to warranty, but the owner is to be given back his own and the additional payment,<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_24-1.whinote.n.1"/> and he who has the right to it is to be given the fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="267" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Yet if the purchased goods had previously been in someone’s possession and the purchaser had no such witnesses, then there can be no vouching to warranty, but the goods must be returned to their owner along with a penalty payment and a fine to the proper authority.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="327"><ref target="clause:IICn_15-2">II Cn 15.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">*vgl. 15, 2</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_45-1">Leis Wl 45.1</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">A's ‘þæt’ should be ‘þam’.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 327, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">327</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">capit. <hi rend="italic">T meist</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">capit. T mostly</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">327</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so KR;</hi> -ra <hi rend="italic">Dm</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus KR; -ra Dm</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.12-2" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gif <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gif Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þil. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þil. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">agife <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">agife Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ꝥ agenfrigean <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ꝥ agenfrigean Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-gyld, ⁊ ða <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi> [<hi rend="italic">vgl. A</hi>]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-gyld, ⁊ ða Ld [cf. A]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> þam</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read þam</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.11-2" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">327</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">guar. <hi rend="italic">Di S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">guar. Di S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.12-3" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">327</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ei non <hi rend="italic">Lb S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ei non Lb S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.13-2" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">327</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">non <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">non added by Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_24-1.lnote.oe.14-2" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">327</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eam <hi rend="italic">nochmals Di</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eam repeated Di</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_24-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">206</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Anefang 12</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Anefang 12</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_24-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">206</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Aftergeld’ auch ECf 26; zu Cons <hi rend="italic">vgl. Wb: prosoluta; persolvere</hi> ‘Busse (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 13b. 14) zahlen’, im Ggs. zu <hi rend="italic">solvere</hi> ‘einfachen Ersatz zahlen’, auch <hi rend="italic">u</hi>. 63²; Domesday I 174a 1. 175b 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘Aftergeld’ also ECf 26; on Cons <hi rend="italic">cf. Wb: prosoluta; persolvere</hi> ‘to pay compensation (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 13b. 14)’, in contrast to <hi rend="italic">solvere</hi> ‘to pay simple restitution’, also <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 63²; Domesday I 174a 1. 175b 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_24-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">206</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Immunitätsherrn (nicht immer dem König), Strafgeldempfänger, vielleicht ohne dass er auch private Gerichtsbarkeit (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 20) übte</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The lord of the immunity (not always the king), the recipient of fines, perhaps without his also exercising private jurisdiction (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 20)</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_24-1.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">355</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">No other instance of the word <hi rend="italic">æftergild</hi> is quoted in BT. (see p. 11, <hi rend="italic">s.v.</hi>). It is translated <hi rend="italic">secundam solutionem</hi> in Q; <hi rend="italic">tantum valens</hi> in Inst.; <hi rend="italic">persolutam</hi> in Cons. Liebermann takes it to mean a payment equal to the value of the goods, cf. the use of <hi rend="italic">persolvere</hi> in IV Atr. 3, 2; II Cn. 63 (where it translates <hi rend="italic">forgyldan</hi> in the three Latin texts).</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_24-1.robnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">186</biblScope></bibl><label>gefó</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">befo</hi> G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="IICn_24-1.whinote.n.1" n="1" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">465</biblScope></bibl><label>payment</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The word <hi rend="italic">æftergyld</hi> is unique. The Latin translators understood it to mean “as much again”.</seg></note>
      </div>
